			],
			"Message": "chore(Land): Sync Land/Element submodules to latest revisions\n\nAdvance all Land/Element submodule references to their current HEADs to maintain build consistency across the editor architecture. This update includes Common, Echo, Maintain, Output, Rest, and SideCar.\n\nThis synchronization incorporates recent PascalCase refactoring, parameter extraction improvements, and build artifact updates generated in the submodules. Ensures the main Land repository aligns with the latest state of its constituent components.",
			"SHA": "b05f7f5389b9ade8bba2b7a73cf5f3e140bff589"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-24T06:25:39Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠇⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				7
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync Land element submodules for build freshness\n\nUpdate all Land/Element submodules to their latest revisions, maintaining consistency across the editor's native backend, UI services, and build tooling.\n\nWind and Cocoon advance their generated artifact timestamps — catalog version dates and RouteManifest.ts compilation timestamp — to match today's codegen cycle. Output and Rest normalize shell script whitespace (tabs to 2-space indentation, pipe alignment, case branch formatting) to enforce script maintenance conventions. Mountain simplifies URI parsing in the ProvideCodeLenses IPC handler by adopting centralized Utilities::Params helpers. Sky and Worker advance to their latest submodule heads with no recorded functional changes in this sync.\n\nAll editor components remain build-consistent with no functional regressions.",
			"SHA": "a611a770ada3ab84a2a3d0c08144156cbd1bf7f8"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-23T16:31:42Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				26,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Atomize state and enforce PascalCase across architecture\n\nSystematically restructure the Mountain backend to satisfy project-wide PascalCase naming conventions and improve modularization. Decompose monolithic state files into atomic modules (e.g., `MapLockError`, `DispatchDeltaWorkspaceFolders`) and rename all state structs to `Struct` to align with the reverse-hierarchical import pattern (`State::Struct`).\n\nEnforce PascalCase naming across Tauri commands, helper functions, and DTOs, including Air client components (`AirClient` → `Struct`), binary build utilities, and all `Vine`/`IPC` layer handlers. Split large service files into single-purpose modules (e.g., `Binary::Initialize`, `ExtensionManagement::Scanner`) to reduce boilerplate and enforce strict naming adherence defined in `CLAUDE.md`.\n\nCallers now use fully qualified paths (e.g., `Binary::Main::Entry::Fn`), significantly improving code clarity and maintainability across the native backend.",
			"SHA": "27f4c3762942c0fe1e3669247b9640fec6447097"
		}
	],
